      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Meritocracy is a flawed concept because it relies on IQ and standardized tests, which are biased and perpetuate inequality. These tests often favor those with access to better education and resources, reinforcing class divisions. Additionally, they fail to account for diverse talents and intelligences, thus marginalizing individuals who excel in non-academic areas. The focus on IQ and standardized testing as measures of merit only benefits the privileged, further entrenching systemic inequality.",
